// Heal-delivery to a living ally, not damage to a foe. `BasicBeam`
// (common/src/states/basic_beam.rs) always resolves its damage against
// `Some(GroupTarget::OutOfGroup)` -- hardcoded, not a RON-configurable
// field -- so it can never land on an ally regardless of the sheet's own
// variant pick. This is the exact situation weave_transfusion.ron
// (transmutation) already hit and documents in full: "`SelfBuff` cannot
// deliver this... Shipped instead as `BasicMelee` using the exact
// touch-ally pattern already shipped for lesser_restoration.ron/
// greater_restoration.ron". Same fix here: `BasicMelee` with
// `attack_effect_target: Some(InGroup)` on a near-inert Stab.
//
// The sheet's self-cost half of the rider ("caster wounds their own life
// essence... cannot be lessened") is dropped rather than modeled with
// `meta.hp_cost`: that field is a Hemomancy-only convention (see
// `AbilityMeta::form`'s own doc comment -- `hp_cost` is the meta-school's
// blood-cost flavor, tied to `Hemomancy(<classic school>)`), not a generic
// Necromancy mechanic, and this is classic Necromancy, not the Hemomancy
// meta-school. The self-sacrifice flavor is represented instead by a
// steeper `energy_cost` than a plain heal of this size would otherwise
// carry. Magnitude scaled up from spare_the_dying.ron's own Heal(20.0) at
// level 0 to this spell's level 3.
BasicMelee(
    energy_cost: 70.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    swing_duration: 0.1,
    hit_timing: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    melee_constructor: (
        kind: Stab(damage: 1, poise: 0, knockback: 0, energy_regen: 0),
        range: 3.0,
        angle: 20.0,
        attack_effect: Some((
            Heal(90.0),
            AttackSource(Melee),
        )),
        attack_effect_target: Some(InGroup),
    ),
    meta: (school: Some(Necromancy), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
